Verifying this copy:

  curl -sSLo uqr.tgz https://registry.npmjs.org/uqr/-/uqr-0.1.3.tgz
  openssl dgst -sha512 -binary uqr.tgz | openssl base64 -A
  tar -xzf uqr.tgz -O package/dist/index.mjs | diff - index.mjs

Why three pins rather than one: the version alone can be republished, the tag
alone can be moved, and the tarball digest alone does not say what upstream
called it. This code runs on every visitor's device, so all three are recorded.

Audited, and the reason each matters on a page whose URL is a credential:

  no network access      the subscription URL never leaves the device
  no DOM access          the encoder returns a matrix; the drawing is ours
  no eval, no Function   nothing is compiled at runtime
  no timers              nothing runs after encode() returns

Only encode() is called. renderSVG, renderANSI, renderUnicode and
renderUnicodeCompact are unused; the file is kept whole so that it can be
diffed against upstream without a normalisation step.
